   "h": "Endotoxin margin depends on your PW feed",
   "nav": "Endotoxin",
   "body": [
    "A still reduces endotoxin by a fixed factor, not to a fixed level, so the margin depends on your Purified Water (PW) feed. The FDA Guide to Inspections of High Purity Water Systems notes that many still fabricators guarantee only a 2.5 to 3 log reduction, and describes stills making WFI above 0.25 EU/mL from poorly treated feed. So we design still and feed as one: the guaranteed reduction sets your PW endotoxin target in the functional specification.",
    "Ph. Eur. 0169 asks for a still with an effective device to prevent the entrainment of droplets. Distillate leaves hot, so it fills a loop circulating above 70 °C, the example EU GMP Annex 1 (2022) gives, without reheating."
